      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hanna City was founded in 1882 and named after William Hanna, president of the Peoria-Farmington Railroad that ran through town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanna_City%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began as a farming community before coal was discovered beneath it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanna_City%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A major coal mine kept Hanna City thriving for more than half a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanna_City%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Remnants of the coal mine, such as an air shaft near the old Grade School, can still be seen today.",
